  "content_en": "8. Please be safe (2) In the face of interests, there are no permanent enemies, let alone permanent friends! Sister Wenjiu felt that this sentence was so right, because there was a living example playing out in front of her at this moment - \"Third sister-in-law, you are here, I thought that the old lady not only exempted your fourth son from paying greetings, but also exempted you.\" In order to please those in power and free herself, Zhen trampled on others wantonly, and did not blush. After finishing her words, she turned to look at the old lady and the second lady, showing an expression of watching a good show. \"Haha... Yes, third brother and sister, I was just wondering.\" The second lady, who had been at loggerheads with the fourth lady just now, also covered her sleeves and chuckled. Although as soon as she entered her husband's house, she was full of ambition and gave birth to two sons in succession. The eldest son was still the eldest son of the Hou family. Her daughter-in-law, Feng, gave birth to the eldest grandson of the Marquis family. She was very popular in front of the old lady. But what troubled Miao was that both of her sons had mediocre qualifications. The eldest son, Wen Chongnian, relied on the influence of the Marquis Mansion to enter the Imperial College. The younger son, Wen Chongri, the third young master of the Hou Mansion, was even more unsatisfied and didn't like studying. He wandered around the city of Bianzhou all day long, making friends and living a casual life. Why, her extremely precious legitimate son was not as good as a concubine, and besides, her son who was taught by a lady from an aristocratic family who was proficient in music, chess, calligraphy, and painting was not as good as the one raised by a merchant, which made her feel so embarrassed. The two sisters-in-law fanned the flames, causing Jiang's face to turn green and white, and she quickly glanced at the old lady. The old lady didn't look at anyone or speak, she just gently put the jade tea cup with chrysanthemum petals on the Kang table. \"Boom -\" A small sound, but like a heavy hammer, all the sounds in the room suddenly stopped. Even the low hiccups of Sister Zhen's biological daughter, who was only nine years old, stopped instantly. She stared at everyone with a pair of big eyes in confusion and horror. Of course, the ones who were most at a loss at this moment were the Jiang family and their daughter. Jiang family's palms were already wet and cold, and she stood stiffly, forgetting even the etiquette of greeting her. And the culprit, Sister Wen Shi, lowered her head in timidity and shame, not daring to express her anger. \"Chuckling...\" At this moment, a burst of laughter suddenly interrupted the silence in the room. Everyone was startled, and then they saw a small figure sneaking in from outside the door curtain, and went straight to Sister Wen Jiu who was standing next to Jiang, \"Where's the puppy? Where's the little duck? I want the duck, I want the puppy...\" It was Brother Bao who was carried out by the eldest mistress Feng after having an unpleasant quarrel with Zhen just now! \"You kid, why are your legs so fast? What little duck, little dog? Call Aunt Nine.\" Then Feng also chased in, scolding her son without any reproach. \"Aunt Jiu,\" Brother Bao immediately shouted, and then raised his young face expectantly to Sister Wen Jiu, \"I also want ducks and puppies.\" \"Brother Bao, don't be naughty, come on - sit down with great-grandmother to warm yourself up!\" Undoubtedly, Brother Bao's sudden arrival broke up the dull tension in the room, and the old lady who had looked solemn just now softened her expression instantly and showed a sincere smile. \"Grandma, there are puppies and ducks hidden in Aunt Ninth's hand, it's like this... like this...\" Brother Bao didn't move. He turned his head and glanced at Li Taijun, then stretched out his fat fingers and made awkward gestures. Brother Bao's cute appearance couldn't help but make everyone laugh, and then they all looked at Sister Wenjiu in unison, with doubts on their faces. \"Brother Bao, be good. Can you please wait a moment before Aunt Ninth greets the old lady and then play with you?\" Facing everyone's gaze, Sister Ninth lowered her head in shock and whispered to Brother Bao. Brother Bao nodded. Jiang, who had lowered his head and stayed there for a long time, moved slightly, turned his eyes, and glanced at Sister Wenjiu in surprise. Sister Wenjiu still had a low-brow expression. Next, Mrs. Jiang paid her respects to the old lady and gave a solemn salute. Although the old lady just let out a low \"hmm\" from her nostrils, she asked Cuiping, another maid next to her, to show Jiang a seat. Jiang couldn't help but breathed a sigh of relief. Ninth Sister and Tenth Sister also paid their respects to the old lady. The old lady smiled and asked the two of them a few questions, but when she waved them away, her probing eyes fell on Ninth Sister. Sister Jiu's face remained calm, but her heart couldn't help but feel moved. Of course, this Brother Bao would not run in to rescue Jiang for no reason. It was under the white terror that she was secretly watching and listening in all directions, looking for a way to resolve the situation, when she suddenly caught a glimpse of a little head poking through the door curtain. She immediately had an idea, and using the shadow cast by the candlelight that had not been extinguished on one side, she quietlyQuietly, he made a few hand shadow poses. Of course, children are the most sensitive to these games, so... But it seems that her little trick has been seen through by her grandmother, a passerby. Hey, the best of all people! But she doesn't regret it, because compared to being seen through, she would rather choose to help her aunt and gain a place in her heart. Passerby A's grandmother is already at this age, and she has long been worried about concubines and aunts. The harm is that she may cause trouble and jealousy after being discovered. But the fate of her and her aunt is in the hands of this aunt. Didn't her aunt explain this to her with practical actions this morning... Just when Sister Ninth was thinking about it, Sister Wen, who had just forgotten the pain after the scar healed, had already begun to discuss homework with the second wife's biological daughter, Fourth Sister Wen. Here, Mrs. Jiang presented to the old lady the candle sent by her parents' family yesterday. Candles were rare items in the past, and the ones sent by the Jiang family were of high quality. The old lady finally became happy with Mrs. Jiang's kindness. The old lady also handed one to the second lady, and the second lady also joined in the conversation, which was quite speculative for a while. Zhen was excluded again and couldn't help but grit her teeth again. The daughter of a lowly merchant was actually more respectable than her, huh... I was hating it, but suddenly I caught a glimpse of my biological daughter Eleven Sister behind me, looking at Sister Ten and Sister Four eagerly. She wanted to interrupt several times, but both of them ignored her. Her fists clenched instantly, and her nails dug into her flesh. \"Sister Ten, tell me, did you fall asleep again this morning and that's why you were late?\" Zhen suddenly said to Sister Ten with a smile on her face. Everyone's eyes also followed this sound, and the room became quiet again... --------- Off topic - Dear friends, collect one,",
